{"title":"Career Roadmap · Smart Systems Designer","role":"Smart Systems Designer","summary":"A Smart Systems Designer designs integrated physical-digital systems that combine mechanical components, sensors, electronics, automation, software, connectivity, and data/AI.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. — Engineering & Technology","Course":"Mechanical Engineering (Smart Mechanical / Mechatronics & Automation)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Smart Systems Designer designs integrated physical-digital systems that combine mechanical components, sensors, electronics, automation, software, connectivity, and data/AI."},{"type":"p","text":"Unlike a traditional mechanical designer who primarily focuses on mechanical components, a smart-systems professional considers the entire connected system:"},{"type":"p","text":"Mechanical System"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Sensors & Electronics"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Embedded Control"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Automation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Software"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Connectivity"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["Data / AI","SMART SYSTEM"]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical applications include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Smart manufacturing equipment"},{"text":"Automated machinery"},{"text":"Industrial IoT systems"},{"text":"Robotic systems"},{"text":"Smart appliances"},{"text":"Connected machines"},{"text":"Predictive-maintenance systems"},{"text":"Automated inspection systems"},{"text":"Smart energy systems"},{"text":"Autonomous equipment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role is interdisciplinary, so job titles may vary. Relevant market titles include Mechatronics Engineer, Systems Engineer, Automation Engineer, Smart Manufacturing Engineer, IoT Engineer, Product Development Engineer, and Robotics Engineer."